        {
            "name": "Menaḥem ben Makhir",
            "bio": "Menaḥem ben Makhir (fl. 11th c.) was German liturgist and a native of Ratisbon. His grandfather, also called Menahem b. Machir, was a nephew of Gershom b. Judah, and he himself was a cousin of Isaac b. Judah, Rashi's teacher. He is quoted in Rashi's \"Pardes\" (21d, 33c) and in the \"Liḳḳuṭe Pardes\" (19b; comp. \"Pisḳe Reḳanaṭi,\" No. 589). Menaḥem witnessed the Jewish massacres of 1096 in Germany and commemorated them in a number of seliḥot. His piyyuṭim include: \"Adam be-ḳum,\" for the Esther fast (quoted in Tos. to Ḥag. 11a); \"Aḥalleh et pene Adonai,\" for Yom Kippur minḥah; \"Amarer ba-beki,\" for the 17th of Tammuz; \"Lammah Adonai ta'amod\" (in ten strophes); a \"ḳinah\" for the 9th of Ab, beginning \"Ebel a'orer\"; five \"yotserot,\" including one for the \"Naḥamu\" Sabbath and one for the \"Shuvah\" Sabbath; three \"ofanim\"; three \"zulatot\"; \"Kehosha'ta elim,\" a \"hosha'na\" for the Sabbath of Tabernacles; \"Ma'ariv,\" for the Feast of Tabernacles; \"Nishmat, to be recited on Simḥat Torah; and a reshut for Ḥatan Torah, to be recited on the same day. Most of his piyyuṭim are alphabetically arranged, but all of them bear the author's signature.",
            "website": "https://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/10632-menahem-ben-machir",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/Keith-Evans-Green-Tree-Yellow-Field-CC-BY-SA-250x250.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/menahem-ben-makhir"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-09-17",
    "last_updated": "2026-09-25",
    "excerpt": "The ofan piyyuṭ for Shabbat Shuva, minhag Polin, by the great payṭan Menaḥem ben Rabbi Makhir. A half-acrostic, each stanza begins with a word from parashat Ha'azinu, usually read on Shabbat Shuva, and ends with a verse that includes the word \"holy\" or \"sanctify\" in it. ",
    "content": "<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\nThe ofan piyyuṭ for Shabbat Shuva, minhag Polin, by the great payṭan Menaḥem ben Rabbi Makhir. A half-acrostic, each stanza begins with a word from parashat Ha&#8217;azinu, usually read on Shabbat Shuva, and ends with a verse that includes the word &#8220;holy&#8221; or &#8220;sanctify&#8221; in it.\n</div>\n<hr />\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\">Source (Hebrew)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Translation (English)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Translation (German)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nהַאֲזִ֥ינוּ <span class=\"acrostic\">אַ</span>בִּירִים בְּנֵי אֵלִים מׄוֹרָא מִקְדָּשׁ כְּמֵהֵֽינוּ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בְּ</span>הַֽדְרַת קֹֽדֶשׁ שִֽׂימוּ פְּנֵיכֶם לְתַלְפִּיּוֹת גׇּבְהֵֽנוּ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">גַּ</span>ם בְּמִקְדָּשׁ מְעַט הַיְשִֽׁירוּ עַפְעַפֵּי גִּיהֵֽנוּ<br />\nוְֽ֭הִשְׁתַּחֲווּ לְהַ֣ר קׇדְשׁ֑וֹ כִּי־קָ֝ד֗וֹשׁ יְהֹוָ֥ה אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃ <span class=\"citation\">(תהלים צט:ט)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nGive ear,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Deuteronomy 32:1&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> awesome children of the divine, our hope in the revered Temple! <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBy the holy Footstool set your faces, to our high spoken-mound. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nGrade straight your lidded eyes in the small sanctuary<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find Ezekiel 11:16. The synagogue.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> as well, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nand bow to <span class=\"divine-referent\">Their</span> holy mountain, for <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Cause</span> <span class=\"divine-referent\">our God</span> is holy! <span class=\"citation\">(Psalms 99:9)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"german\" lang=\"deu-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nHöret, ihr Braven, Söhne der Mächtigen, die ihr euch sehnet nach dem hehren Tempel, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nrichtet euch in heiliger Furcht nach dem hohen Tempelhügel! <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAuch in dem kleinen Heiligtum erhebt zu ihm die Augen <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nund werfet euch nieder vor seinem heiligen Berge; denn heilig ist der Ewige, unser Gott.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nיַעֲרֹ֤ף <span class=\"acrostic\">דֶּֽ</span>בֶב לֶֽקַח לְקוּחָה נֹֽׄפֶת תַּטֵּף לְמׇתְקָהּ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">הָ</span>עֵת יוֹשֶֽׁבֶת בַּגַּנִּים קוֹל קִלּוּס לְוִתְקָהּ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">וְ</span>עוּדִים חֲבֵרִים מַקְשִׁיבִים מַחְשִׁים דְּמִמָּה דַּקָּה<br />\nוַיִּגְבַּ֛הּ יְהֹוָ֥ה צְבָא֖וֹת בַּמִּשְׁפָּ֑ט וְהָאֵל֙ הַקָּד֔וֹשׁ נִקְדָּ֖שׁ בִּצְדָקָֽה׃ <span class=\"citation\">(ישעיה ה:טז)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nLet drip,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[3]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Deuteronomy 32:2&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> dripping like sweet honeycomb, the speech of <span class=\"divine-referent\">God</span>’s taken teaching, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\neven as she sits in the gardens<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[4]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Song of Songs 8:13. Here referring to the people Israel sitting in the synagogue.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> to praise it in beautiful sound, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nand the equal councils<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[5]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> The angelic hosts&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> listen to the still small whispers <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nand <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Cause</span> <span class=\"divine-referent\">our God</span> is high in justice, and <span class=\"divine-referent\">the holy Deity</span> sanctified in justice. <span class=\"citation\">(Isaiah 5:16)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"german\" lang=\"deu-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nEs trieft das Wort der uns geschenkten Gotteslehre süß wie Honigseim, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nzur Zeit, wo die Gemeinde zum Hochgesange sich versammelt, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nund leise flüsternd vereinigen sich die Himmelswesen, um zu lauschen, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nund es erhebt sich der Ewige Zebaoth im Gerichte und geheiligt wird der heilige Gott in Gerechtigkeit.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nכִּ֛י שֵׁ֥ם יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶקְרָ֑א <span class=\"acrostic\">זֶ</span>ה יוֹשֵׁב תְּהִלּוֹת חֵֽׄלֶף גֵּאִיתִיו גֵּאַֽנִי<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חִ</span>ין קְדֻשּׁוֹת שְׁלׇשְׁתָּן לְהִתְפָּאֵר בָּם נִשְּׂאַֽנִי<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">טֶֽ</span>כֶס שְׁתַּֽיִם מֵהֶם גְּמוּל טוֹב הֶרְאֵֽנִי<br />\nוְהִתְקַדִּשְׁתֶּם֙ וִהְיִיתֶ֣ם קְדֹשִׁ֔ים כִּ֥י קָד֖וֹשׁ אָ֑נִי <span class=\"citation\">(ויקרא יא:מד)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nFor the name of <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Cause</span> I call!<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[6]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Deuteronomy 32:3&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> Zeal-seated, for my exaltation I am exalted; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nhow by <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Trisagion</span>’s glorifying grace I am raised. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nTwo of them are shown to me, lain as a good reward: <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAnd be sanctified and be holy, for I am holy.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[7]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> This verse has the word holy in it twice.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"citation\">(Leviticus 11:44)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"german\" lang=\"deu-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWenn ich des Ewigen Namen rufe, der unter Lobgesängen thronet, so erhöhet er mich, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nweil ich ihn erhöhe mit dem Gesange des dreimalheilig; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nzwei davon legt er auf mich, als treffliche Belohnung, wie er dies in den Worten zeigt: <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n„Ihr sollt euch heiligen und heilig sein, denn ich bin heilig!“\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nהַצּוּר֙ <span class=\"acrostic\">יִ</span>דֹּדוּן מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת מְׄרוּצָתָם בְּלִי לַעֲקֹב<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">כִּ</span>וּוּן עֵת רָצוֹן כַּוֵּי רְקִיעִים לִקֹּב<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">לְ</span>הַעֲרִיץ לְהַמְלִיץ סְגֻלָּה מִכְתָּב מְבֹאָר לִנְקֹב<br />\nיַקְדִּ֣ישֽׁוּ שְׁמִ֑י וְהִקְדִּ֙ישׁוּ֙ אֶת־קְד֣וֹשׁ יַֽעֲקֹ֔ב׃ <span class=\"citation\">(ישעיה כט:כג)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span class=\"divine-referent\">The Rock</span>,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[8]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Deuteronomy 32:4&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> You are to whom angelic forces rush without delay; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nconsidering the desired time to pierce the chambers of the firmaments, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nlionizing and defending the chosen, as the writing is clearly interpreted: <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThey will sanctify My <span class=\"divine-referent\">name</span> and sanctify Jacob’s <span class=\"divine-referent\">Holy One</span>. <span class=\"citation\">(Isaiah 29:23)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"german\" lang=\"deu-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nIn unaufgehaltener Eile schweben die Engelsscharen dahin zum Schöpfer, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\ndie Gnadenzeit beachtend, wo die Himmelspforten geöffnet sind, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\num das erkorne Volk kräftig zu verteidigen. So steht ausdrücklich geschrieben: <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n„Diese heiligen meinen Namen und Jene heiligen den Heiligen Jakobs“\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">מְ</span>סֻיָּם בְּאַלְפֵי שִׁנְאָן בִּׄקְדוֹשֵׁי רִׄבֵּׄיׄ רִבּוֹאוֹת<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נ</span>וֹרָא בִּבְנֵי אֵלִים בְּתוֹךְ צְבָאוֹ אוֹת<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">ס</span>וֹבְבִים כִּסֵּא כְּבוֹדוֹ בְּשָׁלֹשׁ כִּתּוֹת לְהַנְאוֹת<br />\nקָד֧וֹשׁ ׀ קָד֛וֹשׁ קָד֖וֹשׁ יְהֹוָ֣ה צְבָא֑וֹת׃ <span class=\"citation\">(ישעיה ו:ג)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nMyriad myriads of holy ones, thousands of millions, but among them, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nnoteworthy among the children of the divine, amid <span class=\"divine-referent\">Their</span> force a sign, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nsurrounding <span class=\"divine-referent\">Their</span> glorious throne in three parties to laud; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHoly, holy, holy is <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Cause of Forces</span>! <span class=\"citation\">(Isaiah 6:3)</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"german\" lang=\"deu-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nErkennbar ist der Herr unter den tausendfältigen Myriaden Heiligen, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\ngefürchtet von allen Götterwesen, ausgezeichnet in seinem Heere. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nSie stehen um den Thron seiner Herrlichkeit in drei Lager geteilt und rufen das liebliche <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n„Heilig, heilig, heilig ist der Ewige Zebaoth“ –\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h3>Source(s)</h3>\n<p><span style=\"float: right;\"><div id=\"attachment_69252\" style=\"width: 260px\" class=\"wp-caption alignleft\"><a href=\"https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/die-piutim-fur-alle-sabbathe-des-jahres-nach-polnischem-ritus-seligman-baer-1862-p--402.png\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-69252\" src=\"https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/upload